Adapted from TheSimpsonsGameRecomp 7deb273b and the same change in the Marvel Ultimate Alliance ReXGlue patch 0106 (the D3D12 half). The vertex buffer residency cache was keyed on guest address and size and kept across draws and frames, so a fetch constant rebound at the same address and size skipped RequestRange, which is the only thing that consults the valid-page table and re-uploads vertex data the CPU rewrote in place: a buffer rebuilt every frame at a fixed address was uploaded once and never again (stale vertices, flicker). Residency is deduplicated within one draw only, as in Xenia. This also removes the invalidation calls of 0053, 0055 and 0044, which only cleared the bits.

